UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Study the Bachelor of Laws and Bachelor of Business to pursue a career as a legal professional or to open the gateway to a wide variety of positions in both the public and private sectors in your chosen business discipline. Choose to complete work-based learning opportunities to enrich your learning experience while benefiting from the flexibility of studying online utilising our renowned online platform.</p><p>On completion, you will be eligible to seek admission as an Australian Legal Practitioner after completing the required professional training (Practical Legal Training Course).</p><p>Register for our <a href="/events/1279548/business-and-accounting-open-day-webinar">Business and Accounting Webinar</a> on Wednesday 26th August</p><p>The Bachelor of Laws and Bachelor of Business is a multidisciplinary qualification designed to enable you to gain entry into the legal profession combined with business knowledge and skills. This course offers innovative and hands-on learning experiences that bridge theory with real-world practice and provide you with the skills and insights needed to thrive in an ever-evolving business landscape. This unique blend of legal and business skills will help set you apart in the competitive job market and prepare you for a dynamic and rewarding career. </p><p>Prepare to excel in an ever-evolving legal landscape with a dynamic online curriculum that blends legal knowledge with practical skills. Experience legal practice in the real-world with our extensive network of industry partners across Australia. From placements in law firms and community legal centres to innovative virtual law offices, you will gain invaluable experience that connects classroom theory with real-life practice. To ensure our students are equipped for the challenges and opportunities presented by the continuous and rapid innovation in technology and artificial intelligence, our degree focuses on the ethical, social and practical implications of these advancements and empowers students to harness the legal tech evolution. Accredited by the Legal Practitioners Admissions Board, the Bachelor of Laws ensures you are ready to become a practising lawyer upon completing the necessary practical training. With mutual recognition of practising certificates throughout the States and Territories, work opportunities throughout Australia are open to our law graduates. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 260,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 105750,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 87000,
    apply_form = 'https://www.cqu.edu.au/courses/cl53/bachelor-of-laws-and-bachelor-of-business',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '052447E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The Graduate Certificate in Research (GCR) is ideal if you are interested in developing research capabilities for your career or seeking a pathway to pursue entry into Higher Degree by Research. This course is aimed at professionals in a range of industry, government and community settings, and the course content is able to be tailored to suit your current employment context and/or areas of research interest.</p><p>This course will provide you the opportunity to build fundamental research and critical inquiry skills. You will learn to analyse and synthesise research literature, develop well-justified research questions, and design appropriate research strategies to address those questions using relevant technologies (including artificial intelligence), where applicable. </p><p>In addition, you will develop skills in research dissemination in written, verbal, and technology-enabled contexts, learning to effectively convey complex ideas to both expert and non-expert audiences. The course emphasises professional and ethical research practices, encouraging collaborative work and reflective learning. While centered on a specific research interest, the course builds transferable research skills rather than focusing on a single methodology or project. This approach ensures you develop broad research capabilities applicable across academic, industry, and community contexts.</p><p>The course is governed by the <a href="https://delivery-cqucontenthub.stylelabs.cloud/api/public/content/graduate-certificate-in-research-course-rules-current-version-from-10-january-2026-938236.pdf">Graduate Certificate in Research Course Rules</a> which provide details regarding all aspects of admission, progression, submission and examination of your thesis.</p><p>Interested in speaking to someone about the Graduate Certificate in Research? <a href="/research/research-higher-degrees/ask-a-question">Book a call back today</a>.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 26,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 13344,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 1184,
    apply_form = 'https://www.cqu.edu.au/courses/cl58/graduate-certificate-in-research',
    updated_at = NOW()
