UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>CQUniversity''''s Master of Construction Management prepares you to meet the current and future challenges of the building industry.</p><p>This course is ideal if you are looking to build your construction management credentials for a career as a Construction Manager and you hold a three-year bachelor degree in areas related to construction such as architecture, building, construction management, engineering or project management. </p><p>Construction Managers plan and organise, and control activities relating to high and low-rise buildings including residential, commercial and government projects. In this course, you will learn about the process of building construction from land planning and building legislation, procurement, risk management, contract administration, and the use of building information modelling (BIM) as it applies to construction.</p><p>As a construction manager, you will apply project management principles throughout the construction project cycle to meet key project performance objectives including time, cost, quality, safety, and sustainability ensuring successful project delivery. You will have the opportunity to gain crucial lifelong learning and transferable generic skills, such as critical thinking and problem-solving. </p><p>In your final year, you will choose one of the following Streams:</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 73680,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 62800,
    apply_form = 'https://www.cqu.edu.au/courses/cl82/master-of-construction-management',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '0101470';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Move into a career in construction management, or enhance your career with the Graduate Diploma of Construction Management from CQUniversity. Learn from industry professionals while completing practical, industry-oriented assessments that can be applied immediately to your current role. </p><p>The Graduate Diploma of Construction Management embeds project management concepts from initiating, planning and leading lean projects to executing and closing projects and develop highly sought-after project management skills. </p><p>You''''ll also develop your knowledge in risk management and legal concepts relevant to contracts, and gain an introduction to modern building construction technology with an emphasis on multi-unit and low-rise construction. </p><p>The Graduate Diploma of Construction Management provides a seamless pathway into our <a href="/courses/700060/master-of-construction-management">Master of Construction Management</a>, allowing you to build your skills and knowledge further and receive credit for the units you have already completed. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 35130,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 32100,
